RSX_PERF=1: opt-in per-second host timing of the FIFO walker, D3D12 submit/present and the main thread's waits.

Diagnostic for the performance probe, off by default (one getenv, cached). With RSX_PERF=1 a reporter thread,
started by the first FIFO walk, prints once per second:
- [perf]: guest flip requests, FIFO flips consumed by live-draw, presents, live-draw draws; FIFO walk count and
  time (cellGcm_rsx_process_fifo, includes live-draw method work); D3D12 flushes by reason (present, guest
  reference, other) with their total time and the GPU-fence wait inside them; whole present time and the
  IDXGISwapChain::Present call alone; ref-register polls; real time in sys_timer_usleep of the thread that
  called cellGcmInit (count, ms) and of all other threads.
- [perf-wait]: the cellGcmInit thread's usleep time per guest call site (lr), top 4.
- [perf-thr]: process CPU and the 10 busiest host threads (CPU ms in the last second), labelled rsx (walker/
  present thread), gcm-init, ppu:<guest name>, or tid@+RVA of the thread start in the exe / tid@module+off.
RSX_PERF_SAMPLE=1 adds an instruction-pointer sampler over the threads that used >= 300 ms CPU in the previous
second (suspend, GetThreadContext, resume every 5 ms; nothing else while suspended) and prints the top 64
256-byte RVA buckets per thread every 10 s ([perf-samp]); resolve them offline against the exe's symbols.
LD_PRESENT_INTERVAL=0..4 sets the swap-chain sync interval of the live-draw present (default 1).

Rebased on ps3recomp v0.18.0 (SPU pass 108): drain: upstream's wprof_note_walker + g_gcm_drain_tid before 2007's perf split; sys_timer both.

